  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Maintenance and reliability release.\n\nFixed:\n- GraphQL: a malformed or message-less `errors` array could throw KeyNotFoundException/InvalidOperationException instead of a BigDataCloudException, masking the real API error. All error entries are now surfaced.\n- GraphQL: the API returns validation errors with HTTP 400, which previously produced an unhelpful generic failure. Errors are now parsed before the status code is considered.\n- REST: a non-success response consumed the body as a stream after it had already been opened, which could yield an empty ResponseBody on some platforms.\n- REST: deserialisation failures now throw BigDataCloudException with context instead of a raw JsonException.\n\nAdded:\n- BigDataCloudException.ApiDescription surfaces the API's own `description` field (e.g. \"access denied or your quota limit has been exceeded\").\n- User-Agent header identifying the SDK and runtime version.\n- Automatic gzip/deflate decompression, reducing bandwidth on large payloads such as ip-geolocation-full.\n\nNo breaking API changes.",
